BT /F2 8.80 Tf 0.120 0.140 0.170 rg 63.00 828.00 Td (users carries no credentials.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 63.00 813.00 Td (Phase 1 ships without authentication by explicit decision, so there is no password, hash or session column anywhere in the schema. The table exists to satisfy the PRD's user_id metadata requirement) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 63.00 802.00 Td (and to give real auth somewhere to attach later.) Tj ET
0.130 0.290 0.550 rg
40.00 770.50 15.00 13.00 re
f
BT /F2 7.40 Tf 1.000 1.000 1.000 rg 45.32 774.00 Td (2) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.80 Tf 0.120 0.140 0.170 rg 63.00 774.00 Td (datasets.id doubles as the physical storage UUID.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 63.00 759.00 Td (The storage key is {company_id}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{dataset_id}.{ext}. The original filename is kept in original_filename as metadata only and never contributes a character to a filesystem path \(PRD) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 63.00 748.00 Td (principle 2\).) Tj ET
0.130 0.290 0.550 rg
40.00 716.50 15.00 13.00 re
f
BT /F2 7.40 Tf 1.000 1.000 1.000 rg 45.32 720.00 Td (3) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.80 Tf 0.120 0.140 0.170 rg 63.00 720.00 Td (Two different 'status' concepts, deliberately separated.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 63.00 705.00 Td (datasets.status is the pipeline state \(pending_upload, uploaded, validating, profiling, profiled, analysis_ready, plus terminal upload_failed / profiling_failed / blocked\). dataset_profiles.quality_status is) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 63.00 694.00 Td (the validation verdict \(pass / warning / blocked\). The PRD never enumerated either.) Tj ET
0.130 0.290 0.550 rg
40.00 662.50 15.00 13.00 re
f
BT /F2 7.40 Tf 1.000 1.000 1.000 rg 45.32 666.00 Td (4) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.80 Tf 0.120 0.140 0.170 rg 63.00 666.00 Td (datasets.quality_state is a denormalised copy.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 63.00 651.00 Td (It mirrors the newest structural schema_validations.state so the dataset list can filter on quality without a join. schema_validations remains the source of truth.) Tj ET
0.130 0.290 0.550 rg
40.00 619.50 15.00 13.00 re
f
BT /F2 7.40 Tf 1.000 1.000 1.000 rg 45.32 623.00 Td (5) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.80 Tf 0.120 0.140 0.170 rg 63.00 623.00 Td (column_profiles.dataset_id is denormalised too.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 63.00 608.00 Td (The authoritative parent is dataset_profile_id. Carrying dataset_id as well lets KPI-candidate queries rank columns without joining through dataset_profiles. Both are ON DELETE CASCADE, so the two) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 63.00 597.00 Td (paths cannot disagree.) Tj ET
0.130 0.290 0.550 rg
805.00 824.50 15.00 13.00 re
f
BT /F2 7.40 Tf 1.000 1.000 1.000 rg 810.32 828.00 Td (6) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.80 Tf 0.120 0.140 0.170 rg 828.00 828.00 Td (Per-column statistics are rows, not a JSON blob.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 828.00 813.00 Td (One row per column lets the KPI candidate query rank in SQL and lets the Columns tab paginate server-side. Only the type-specific statistics - percentiles, top_values, datetime_stats, whose shapes) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 828.00 802.00 Td (differ entirely between numeric, categorical and datetime columns - stay in JSON.) Tj ET
0.130 0.290 0.550 rg
805.00 770.50 15.00 13.00 re
f
BT /F2 7.40 Tf 1.000 1.000 1.000 rg 810.32 774.00 Td (7) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.80 Tf 0.120 0.140 0.170 rg 828.00 774.00 Td (kpi_definitions stores the contract twice, on purpose.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 828.00 759.00 Td (The typed columns drive validation and queries; definition holds the frozen, source-agnostic JSON contract handed to the RCA engine in exactly the shape PRD section 11 specifies. The service is the) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 828.00 748.00 Td (single writer and builds the JSON from the columns.) Tj ET
0.130 0.290 0.550 rg
805.00 716.50 15.00 13.00 re
f
BT /F2 7.40 Tf 1.000 1.000 1.000 rg 810.32 720.00 Td (8) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.80 Tf 0.120 0.140 0.170 rg 828.00 720.00 Td (schema_validations is append-only.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 828.00 705.00 Td (Users re-upload corrected files and need to see what changed, so results accumulate rather than being overwritten. mode distinguishes a structural run from one re-checked against a specific KPI) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 828.00 694.00 Td (definition, which is why kpi_definition_id is nullable.) Tj ET
0.130 0.290 0.550 rg
805.00 662.50 15.00 13.00 re
f
BT /F2 7.40 Tf 1.000 1.000 1.000 rg 810.32 666.00 Td (9) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.80 Tf 0.120 0.140 0.170 rg 828.00 666.00 Td (sql_connections has no plaintext password column.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 828.00 651.00 Td (password_encrypted holds a versioned Fernet token \('v1:' prefix\) produced by app.core.security. The API read schema has no password field at all, so a credential cannot leak through a response even) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 828.00 640.00 Td (by mistake.) Tj ET
0.130 0.290 0.550 rg
805.00 608.50 15.00 13.00 re
f
BT /F2 7.40 Tf 1.000 1.000 1.000 rg 808.14 612.00 Td (10) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.80 Tf 0.120 0.140 0.170 rg 828.00 612.00 Td (JSON columns are portable across dialects.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.80 Tf 0.320 0.350 0.400 rg 828.00 597.00 Td (Every JSON column is declared JSON\(\).with_variant\(JSONB, 'postgresql'\). Production keeps JSONB; the test suite runs the identical schema against SQLite.) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.40 Tf 0.420 0.460 0.520 rg 40.00 34.00 Td (Source of truth: backend/app/db/models/  -  regenerate with  python scripts/generate_erd.py) Tj ET
